1370 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: I'm ready to cast the tetragon. It's a magic barrier that can\repel even the strongest northern sorcery. As long as you don't leave it,\you'll be fine.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1380 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: What if they brought weapons? It might stop a spell, but I doubt it'll\stop a bullet.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1390 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: The King of the North will be casting his curse, so he won't be\coming here personally. Whoever comes here will know that I'm casting a\spell, so they'll try to kill me.":GOSUB 5100
1400 BM$="Susanna: While they're distracted, you should stab them with this dagger\and look at their blood. I'm a dark sorceress - I'm more than glad to\sacrifice myself to stop the King of the North.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1410 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: So you're just going to die...? Screw that! I'd rather run if I have to\lose you to defeat the King of the North!":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1420 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: It's not like I want to die. King Hroth will save me if he thinks he\needs me. That's why I must be ready for anything to win.":GOSUB 5100
1430 GOSUB 9575:GOSUB 5510:GOSUB 9506:BM$="Susanna closed the door, picked up a dagger from the altar, and gave it to\David.":GOSUB 5100
1440 BM$="Susanna: This is a cursed dagger. A single scratch, and all blood will gush\out from their body. Can you do it?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1450 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: I don't think I can go for the vitals, but if I just need to scratch them\anywhere I should be fine. Susanna, please... Don't get yourself killed.":GOSUB 5100
1460 COMMON FO:BM$="David: Do you think Mr. Lands is fine...?":GOSUB 5100
1461 GOSUB 9020:'
1465 GOSUB 9050:GOSUB 6210:BM$="David: Urgh! M-My body... My veins feel... burning... ARGH!":GOSUB 5100
1470 BM$="Susanna: It's the curse of the King of the North! David, remember the plan!":GOSUB 5100
1480 GOSUB 6200:GOSUB 9525:BM$="Susanna started chanting her spell, and David's pain subsided.":GOSUB 5100
1490 GOSUB 6190:BM$="While David could hear Susanna's spell, he could not hear the King of the\North's chant.":GOSUB 5100
1500 BM$="After some time, Susanna's forehead was beaded with sweat. Her chant\seemed to be losing intensity.":GOSUB 5100
1510 GOSUB 6220:BM$="David stared at the door, dagger at the ready, but nobody seemed intent\on opening it... Then, someone screamed beyond the door.":GOSUB 5100
1520 BM$="David thought it was the voice of Lands. His ambush must have failed, and\he had been killed...":GOSUB 5100
1530 GOSUB 9545:BM$="Then he heard the footsteps of multiple people coming down the stairs.\Lands had successfully led them their way.":GOSUB 5100
1540 POLL X:GOSUB 9505:BM$="The door quaked with a dull sound. The northern tribesmen were ramming\it. On the third strike, the door gave in.":GOSUB 5100
1550 GOSUB 6230:BM$="In order to protect Susanna, David was prepared to kill whoever came in\first... But nobody did. He looked at Susanna, who was still chanting her\spell.":GOSUB 5100
1560 GOSUB 9535:BM$="Then, a metal lump rolled across the floor, stopping near them. It was\followed by more metal lumps.":GOSUB 5100
1570 GOSUB 6240:BM$="Suddenly, a series of explosions rocked the basement. The metal lumps had\been grenades. Neither David nor Susanna had time to realize it before\the explosion enveloped them.":GOSUB 5100
1580 COMMON FO:POLL X:GOSUB 9566:GOSUB 6250:ISET X:GOSUB 9030:BM$="A man came down the stairs. It was Archbishop Mellis of St. Radford's\Church... also known as the King of the North.":GOSUB 5100:'
1590 BM$="King of the North: Fools. Spells are not necessarily your best assets... We\live in the age of science. In modern warfare, victory goes to whoever\employs the best weapons.":GOSUB 5100
1600 BM$="King of the North: This was never a battle of good versus evil. Its only\purpose was severing once and for all the blood of the King of the North,\or the blood of the Devil King.":GOSUB 5100:BM$="King of the North: Now that the blood of the Devil King is no more, mine has\lost its meaning.":GOSUB 5100
1610 BM$="King of the North: I have brought an end to an ancient battle that has\continued for centuries. As a servant of God, I have slain not men, but dark\demons.":GOSUB 5100
1620 BM$="King of the North: Let us leave. Tonight we will dream of the death of the\demon. Tomorrow we will wake up, and in time forget...":GOSUB 5100
1630 GOSUB 9566:BM$="The King of the North and his followers went up the stairs. In the\basement, nothing was left of David and Susanna...":GOSUB 5100
1640 COMMON FO:ISET X:GOSUB 6260:GOSUB 9000:BM$="The cars of the northern tribesmen were gone. Illuminated by starlight,\the castle seemingly floated alone in the darkness.":GOSUB 5100
1650 GOSUB 9070:GOSUB 6270:BM$="In a corner of the sky, one star was rapidly losing its light, as if mourning\the loss of its master.":GOSUB 5100
1660 GOSUB 6296:BM$="It was like a broken mirror, whose fragments were sinking into the depths\of the ocean... Drifting deeper, and deeper...":GOSUB 5100
